This license covers the code in engine/ and the figure scripts. Each text in
papers/ keeps its own license, recorded in papers/<name>/meta.yaml:

- papers/bitcoin: "Bitcoin: A Peer-to-Peer Electronic Cash System",
  © 2008 Satoshi Nakamoto, MIT license (bitcoin.org). Text adapted from
  github.com/karask/satoshi-paper.
- papers/rfc-1925: "The Twelve Networking Truths", R. Callon, 1996.
  "Distribution of this memo is unlimited."
- papers/zen-of-python: "PEP 20: The Zen of Python", Tim Peters, 2004.
  "This document has been placed in the public domain."
- papers/rfc-791: "Internet Protocol", RFC 791, J. Postel, Editor, 1981,
  excerpt (section 3.1). No copyright notice; "All RFCs may be freely
  reproduced and translated (unmodified)" (www.rfc-editor.org/faq).
- papers/snow-cholera-map: map by John Snow, 1854, public domain (scan from
  the UCLA Department of Epidemiology via Wikimedia Commons). The notice is
  not a period text: it was written for this poster and falls under the MIT
  license above.

